## Best Practices

### Discover Before Acting

Call `get_solution_info` first. It returns the selected run profile, which most Solution Runner operations depend on. It does not list the applications, containers or tasks of that profile, so ask the user for the exact name when you don't have it, or read the run profile in ABP Studio.

### Target Applications Explicitly

`start_applications` and `stop_applications` take `apps` (an array of names), `folder` (everything under a folder) or `root: true` (everything from the root). `root` does not affect containers, use the container tools for those.

### Respect Timeouts

`run_task` accepts `timeout_seconds` (default: 300). Increase it for long operations. On timeout the call returns, but the task keeps running in the background.

### Filter Monitor Data

All monitor tools accept `app` to filter by application and `last` to limit the number of entries. `get_logs` also accepts `level`, and `get_requests` accepts `status` and `urlContains`. When debugging a specific service, always filter by app name to reduce noise.

