## Quick Reference: Common Scenarios

| User Says | Tool Sequence |
|---|---|
| "What does this solution look like?" | `get_solution_info` -> `list_modules` -> `list_packages` |
| "Start the application" | `get_solution_info` -> `start_applications` |
| "Start infrastructure" | `start_containers` |
| "What errors are happening?" | `get_exceptions` |
| "Check application logs" | `get_logs` with `app` and optionally `level: "Error"` |
| "Show me the API calls" | `get_requests` |
| "Build and restart" | `dotnet_build` -> `start_applications` |
| "Run database migration" | `run_task` |

---

## Error Handling

A response is flagged with `isError: true` only when its text starts with `Error:`. A failed build or a failed task comes back as a normal response, so always read the text instead of relying on the flag. Common error patterns:

- **"No solution is open"** -- The user needs to open a solution in ABP Studio first
- **"No run profile selected"** -- The user needs to select a run profile in ABP Studio
- **"Applications not found"** / **"Containers not found"** -- The name is wrong, ask the user for the exact one
- **"Build FAILED."** -- Read the build output in the response, it is not flagged as an error
- **"Timed out"** -- Increase `timeout_seconds` or check if the operation is stuck
